        "original_id": "fdc8824b-42e1-58b7-915d-fc2537c961fc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anna Kournikova, Martina Hingis, Jana Novotná, Natasha Zvereva, Lindsay Davenport, Mary Pierce, Serena Williams, Venus Williams, Bob Harper, Dolvett Quince\n- Events: 1999 French Open – Women's Doubles\n- TV Shows: The Biggest Loser (season 12)\n- Roles: professional tennis player, trainer\n\nFacts:\n- Anna Kournikova was born on 7 June 1981.\n- Anna Kournikova is a Russian former professional tennis player.\n- At the 1999 French Open women's doubles event, Jana Novotná partnered with Natasha Zvereva as the first seed.\n- At the 1999 French Open women's doubles event, Martina Hingis partnered with Anna Kournikova as the second seed.\n- At the 1999 French Open women's doubles event, Jana Novotná and Natasha Zvereva retired in their quarterfinal match against Lindsay Davenport and Mary Pierce.\n- At the 1999 French Open women's doubles event, Martina Hingis and Anna Kournikova reached the final.\n- At the 1999 French Open women's doubles final, Serena Williams and Venus Williams defeated Martina Hingis and Anna Kournikova 6–3, 6–7, 8–6.\n- In The Biggest Loser season 12, Anna Kournikova and Dolvett Quince joined existing trainer Bob Harper as trainers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
